---
import "../styles/sv.css";
// Application snippets executed step by step. The Quant recorder (src/scripts/sim.ts) reproduces
// reflex-quant 1.2.0's callback order and output on every scenario; "naive" is a run-on-read
// runtime with recursive push, for comparison.
import { SCENARIOS } from "../scripts/sim";
---
<figure class="sv" data-stackviz>
  <div class="sv-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Example">
    {SCENARIOS.map((s, k) => <button type="button" data-sc={s.id} aria-pressed={k === 0 ? "true" : "false"}>{s.title}</button>)}
  </div>
  <div class="sv-tabs sv-modes" role="group" aria-label="Runtime">
    <span class="sv-blurb"></span>
    <button type="button" data-mode="quant" aria-pressed="true">Reflex Quant</button>
    <button type="button" data-mode="naive" aria-pressed="false">Naive runtime</button>
  </div>
  <div class="sv-graph" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <p class="sv-note" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <div class="sv-cols">
    <div class="sv-col">
      <div class="sv-h sv-left-h"></div>
      <div class="sv-left"></div>
      <div class="sv-meter"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sv-col">
      <div class="sv-h">Your code</div>
      <pre class="sv-code sv-app"></pre>
      <div class="sv-log" aria-label="Console output"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sv-ctl">
    <button type="button" data-sv="reset" aria-label="Restart">⏮</button>
    <button type="button" data-sv="prev" aria-label="Previous step">◀</button>
    <button type="button" data-sv="play">▶ Play</button>
    <button type="button" data-sv="next" aria-label="Next step">▶|</button>
    <span class="sv-count"></span>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    The Quant run is recorded from a model of the kernel and host that reproduces reflex-quant 1.2.0 on every example:
    the same callbacks, in the same order, with the same output. <code>stack[]</code> holds edges: a <em>sibling</em> the
    push will come back to, or the <em>way back</em> up a pull. Edges in the graph are the live dependencies, so a branch
    switch adds and drops them. The naive runtime re-runs whatever is stale when read, nesting closures, and has no cutoff.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
  import "../scripts/stackviz";
</script>
